223	<header>
224	  <h1>hybrid_sim - Core Architecture</h1>
225	  <div class="sub">Andes RISC-V co-simulator: QEMU 9.x (functional, MHz) + vsim (Verilator, cycle-accurate) share architectural state across a magic-CSR boundary.</div>
226	  <div class="legend">
227	    <span><span class="dot qemu"></span>QEMU (TCG functional)</span>
228	    <span><span class="dot vsim"></span>vsim / Verilator (cycle-accurate)</span>
229	    <span><span class="dot abi"></span>Shared ABI / transport</span>
230	  </div>
231	</header>
232	
233	<main>
234	
235	<!-- =================================================== TOP DIAGRAM =================================================== -->
236	<section>
237	  <h2>1. Three-phase round-trip</h2>
238	  <p>Execution starts in QEMU for fast forward, hands off to vsim at a trigger for the cycle-accurate region of interest, then hands back to a fresh QEMU to finish. Click each box to see what it contains.</p>
239	
240	  <div class="arch" id="arch">
241	    <div class="node qemu" data-id="qemu1">
242	      <div class="label">Phase 1 - functional</div>
243	      <div class="title">QEMU 1</div>
244	      <ul>
245	        <li>TCG plugin matches entry trigger</li>
246	        <li>Drains GPR/FPR/CSR/V from gdbstub</li>
247	        <li>Writes <code>hybrid_state_v1</code>, exits</li>
248	      </ul>
249	    </div>
250	    <div class="arrow">
251	      <span class="cap">hybrid_state_v1</span>
252	      <svg viewBox="0 0 100 28" preserveAspectRatio="none">
253	        <defs><marker id="m1" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="5" refY="3" orient="auto">
254	          <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 z" fill="#f0883e"/></marker></defs>
255	        <line x1="0" y1="14" x2="92" y2="14" stroke="#f0883e" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#m1)"/>
256	      </svg>
257	      <span class="file">state file (atomic write)</span>
258	    </div>
259	
260	    <div class="node vsim" data-id="vsim">
261	      <div class="label">Phase 2 - cycle-accurate</div>
262	      <div class="title">vsim (Verilator)</div>
263	      <ul>
264	        <li><code>HandoffController</code> orchestrates</li>
265	        <li><code>ResumeDriver</code> restores via DM</li>
266	        <li>RTL runs; <code>StateDrain</code> captures on exit</li>
267	      </ul>
268	    </div>
269	
270	    <div class="arrow">
271	      <span class="cap">hybrid_state_v1</span>
272	      <svg viewBox="0 0 100 28" preserveAspectRatio="none">
273	        <defs><marker id="m2" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" refX="5" refY="3" orient="auto">
274	          <path d="M0,0 L6,3 L0,6 z" fill="#f0883e"/></marker></defs>
275	        <line x1="0" y1="14" x2="92" y2="14" stroke="#f0883e" stroke-width="2" marker-end="url(#m2)"/>
276	      </svg>
277	      <span class="file">gdbstub P-packets</span>
278	    </div>
279	
280	    <div class="node qemu" data-id="qemu2">
281	      <div class="label">Phase 3 - functional</div>
282	      <div class="title">QEMU 2</div>
283	      <ul>
284	        <li>Spawned with <code>-gdb -S</code></li>
285	        <li>State restored via P-packets</li>
286	        <li>Continues; exit code propagates</li>
287	      </ul>
288	    </div>
289	  </div>
290	
291	  <div id="archDetail" class="detail">
292	    <h3>Click a phase above to inspect its internals.</h3>
293	    <p style="color: var(--muted)">Each phase exchanges the same <code>hybrid_state_v1</code> struct (defined in <code>include/hybrid/state_abi.h</code>), but uses a completely different transport at each boundary: a binary file (QEMU1 to vsim) and the GDB Remote Serial Protocol (vsim to QEMU2). The shared mmap (<code>/dev/shm</code>) is also live in tier-2 fixtures so the C heap/stack survives across all three phases.</p>
294	  </div>
295	</section>
296	
297	<!-- =================================================== COMPONENT CARDS =================================================== -->
298	<section>
299	  <h2>2. Core components</h2>
300	  <p>Click each card to expand. The QEMU side is one C plugin loaded into upstream QEMU; the vsim side is a set of header-only C++20 classes orchestrated by a simulator main loop.</p>
301	
302	  <details open>
303	    <summary><span class="tag qemu">QEMU</span> qemu_plugin / hybrid_handoff.c - drain on trigger</summary>
304	    <div class="grid">
305	      <div class="card">
306	        <h4>Trigger detection</h4>
307	        <p>Translation-time callback (<code>vcpu_tb_trans</code>) inspects every 4-byte insn in the block.</p>
308	        <ul>
309	          <li><b>CSR mode (default):</b> matches <code>csrwi 0x7C0, 0</code> for enter and <code>csrwi 0x7C0, 1</code> for exit. CSR 0x7C0 is a vendor write that has no architectural effect on Andes ax45mp - hence the "magic" trigger.</li>
310	          <li><b>PC mode:</b> when the plugin is loaded with <code>enter_pc=0x...</code>, the CSR matcher is bypassed and only that exact vaddr fires (works on compressed insns via <code>qemu_plugin_insn_size</code>).</li>
311	        </ul>
312	      </div>
313	      <div class="card">
314	        <h4>Register harvest</h4>
315	        <p>On trigger, <code>resolve_handles()</code> looks up every gdbstub register by name. The lookup is lazy because QEMU only registers the dynamic coprocessor features (FPU, V, CSR) after vcpu_init.</p>
316	        <ul>
317	          <li>32 GPR + 32 FPR + PC</li>
318	          <li>13 M-mode CSRs (<code>mstatus</code>, <code>mepc</code>, <code>mtvec</code>, ..., <code>satp</code>)</li>
319	          <li>16 <code>pmpcfg</code> + 64 <code>pmpaddr</code></li>
320	          <li>V CSRs (<code>vstart</code>, <code>vtype</code>, <code>vl</code>, <code>vlenb</code>, <code>vxsat</code>, <code>vxrm</code>, <code>vcsr</code>) + v0..v31 (bytes)</li>
321	        </ul>
322	      </div>
323	      <div class="card">
324	        <h4>PC sourcing quirk</h4>
325	        <p>The PC value comes from <code>compute_handoff_pc(site)</code> using the translation-time vaddr + insn size, <i>not</i> from the gdbstub PC register. Reason: TCG defers PC writes - after a V-extension instruction retires the live gdbstub PC can briefly lag the actual current insn.</p>
326	      </div>
327	      <div class="card">
328	        <h4>Atomic state write</h4>
329	        <p><code>write_state_atomic()</code> writes to <code>$outfile.tmp.$pid</code>, <code>fsync</code>s, then <code>rename()</code>s. The vsim side never sees a torn struct. After write, QEMU calls <code>exit(0)</code>.</p>
330	      </div>
331	    </div>
332	    <div class="file-ref">qemu_plugin/hybrid_handoff.c, include/hybrid/insn_match.h, include/hybrid/state_abi.h</div>
333	  </details>
334	
335	  <details>
336	    <summary><span class="tag vsim">vsim</span> HandoffController - phase dispatcher</summary>
337	    <div class="grid">
338	      <div class="card">
339	        <h4>Role</h4>
340	        <p>Glues <code>CsrTrigger</code> (decoder of magic CSRs) and <code>StateDrain</code>. The Verilator run-loop calls <code>on_retire(pc, gpr_probe)</code> once per committed PC.</p>
341	      </div>
342	      <div class="card">
343	        <h4>Decisions</h4>
344	        <ul>
345	          <li><b>HYBRID_HANDOFF_ENTER</b> - QEMU's job, vsim ignores</li>
346	          <li><b>HYBRID_HANDOFF_EXIT</b> - fire drain</li>
347	          <li><b>HYBRID_HANDOFF_RUNTIME</b> - read rs1 GPR, fire only if value==1</li>
348	        </ul>
349	      </div>
350	      <div class="card">
351	        <h4>Passthrough merge</h4>
352	        <p>The vsim DM cannot read every CSR/V byte cheaply. <code>set_passthrough_input(qemu1_state)</code> caches the QEMU1 snapshot; on drain, <code>drain_with_passthrough</code> overwrites only the fresh fields (GPRs, PC, six V CSRs) and keeps the rest as-is.</p>
353	      </div>
354	      <div class="card">
355	        <h4>Exit code</h4>
356	        <p>When drain fires, the simulator writes the state file and exits with <code>EXIT_HANDOFF_TO_QEMU</code>. The <code>main()</code> wrapper interprets that and invokes <code>run_qemu_handback</code>.</p>
357	      </div>
358	    </div>
359	    <div class="file-ref">verilator/src/hybrid/handoff_controller.hpp</div>
360	  </details>
361	
362	  <details>
363	    <summary><span class="tag vsim">vsim</span> ResumeDriver - restore state via Debug Module</summary>
364	    <div class="grid">
365	      <div class="card">
366	        <h4>Transport: RISC-V Debug Module</h4>
367	        <p>The vsim CPU model exposes a Debug Module over a DMI bus. <code>ResumeDriver</code> only knows about a 32-bit register interface (<code>DmiBus::write/read</code>) - SystemC details are not in this header. This makes the class trivially unit-testable with a fake bus.</p>
368	      </div>
369	      <div class="card">
370	        <h4>Two-tier CSR restore</h4>
371	        <ul>
372	          <li><b>Tier A</b> - Abstract Command writes for GPRs, DPC, mstatus.VS, vstart, vxsat, vxrm, vcsr.</li>
373	          <li><b>Tier B</b> - Program Buffer for V config: stage vl in x5, vtype in x6, then run <code>vsetvl x0, x5, x6</code>. Direct csrrw to vtype would set <code>vill</code>; vl is read-only.</li>
374	        </ul>
375	      </div>
376	      <div class="card">
377	        <h4>Strict ordering</h4>
378	        <p>Order matters because of side effects:</p>
379	        <ol style="margin:0; padding-left:18px; font-size:13px">
380	          <li>dmactive 0 to 1, halt, wait <code>allhalted</code></li>
381	          <li>mstatus.VS (enables V in hart)</li>
382	          <li>vsetvl via PB (resets vstart to 0)</li>
383	          <li>vstart, vxsat, vxrm, vcsr (AFTER vsetvl)</li>
384	          <li>GPR loop x1..x31, DPC (overwrites x5/x6 scratch - safe now)</li>
385	          <li>mtvec tolerant, clear cmderr, resumereq</li>
386	        </ol>
387	      </div>
388	      <div class="card">
389	        <h4>cmderr tolerance</h4>
390	        <p>The Debug Spec makes <code>abstractcs.cmderr</code> sticky. A failed write of an unimplemented CSR would block every subsequent command. The driver checks cmderr after each write, W1C-clears it, and either retries via Program Buffer (<code>write_csr_abstract_or_pb</code>) or treats the slot as a no-op (<code>write_csr_tolerant</code>).</p>
391	      </div>
392	    </div>
393	    <div class="file-ref">verilator/src/hybrid/resume_driver.hpp, abstract_command.hpp, program_buffer.hpp, dmi_poll.hpp</div>
394	  </details>
395	
396	  <details>
397	    <summary><span class="tag vsim">vsim</span> StateDrain - capture on exit trigger</summary>
398	    <div class="grid">
399	      <div class="card">
400	        <h4>What it reads</h4>
401	        <p>Reuses ResumeDriver's DM constants. Halts the hart, reads x1..x31 + DPC via Abstract Commands. FPR/CSR/PMP/V byte arrays are not re-read from the DM - they come from the cached QEMU1 snapshot.</p>
402	      </div>
403	      <div class="card">
404	        <h4>drain_with_passthrough</h4>
405	        <p>When <code>HYBRID_FLAG_V</code> is set, also freshly reads the six scalar V CSRs (<code>vstart</code>, <code>vxsat</code>, <code>vxrm</code>, <code>vcsr</code>, <code>vtype</code>, <code>vl</code>). The 32 V data registers come back via the shared scratch RAM, not via DM.</p>
406	      </div>
407	      <div class="card">
408	        <h4>Error model</h4>
409	        <p>If the DM raises cmderr on a register read, that field is reported as <code>0</code> after a W1C clear, and the next read proceeds. A missing CSR mirrors as zero rather than corrupting the adjacent slot.</p>
410	      </div>
411	      <div class="card">
412	        <h4>Pure-logic split</h4>
413	        <p>The class only touches a <code>DmiBus&amp;</code>. Tests use <code>recording_bus.hpp</code> doctest fixtures to verify the exact DMI write/read sequence without needing SystemC or Verilator.</p>
414	      </div>
415	    </div>
416	    <div class="file-ref">verilator/src/hybrid/state_drain.hpp</div>
417	  </details>
418	
419	  <details>
420	    <summary><span class="tag vsim">vsim</span> qemu_handback - spawn QEMU 2 and replay via gdbstub</summary>
421	    <div class="grid">
422	      <div class="card">
423	        <h4>Spawn</h4>
424	        <p><code>spawn_qemu()</code> forks, redirects stdin to /dev/null (so QEMU's <code>tcsetattr</code> can't SIGTTOU the parent), and execs:</p>
425	        <pre style="margin:6px 0; background:var(--code-bg); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; padding:8px; font-size:11px; overflow-x:auto">qemu-system-riscv64 \
426	  -cpu andes-ax45mpv,vlen=512 -bios none -nographic \
427	  -semihosting-config enable=on,target=native \
428	  -gdb tcp::PORT -S \
429	  [tier-1] -kernel ELF \
430	  [tier-2] -object memory-backend-file,share=on,... -machine andes_ae350,memory-backend=mem</pre>
431	      </div>
432	      <div class="card">
433	        <h4>Register-map discovery</h4>
434	        <p><code>discover_reg_map()</code> walks <code>target.xml</code> and every <code>xi:include</code> annex via <code>qXfer:features:read</code> (chunked because the CSR XML is ~6 KB and PacketSize is ~1000). The result is a register-name to packet-number map - the same names the QEMU plugin used on phase 1.</p>
435	      </div>
436	      <div class="card">
437	        <h4>State application</h4>
438	        <p><code>apply_state()</code> sends P-packets for every field. Each call is silently skipped if the register name is not advertised (some QEMU builds omit PMP slots or extension CSRs).</p>
439	        <ul>
440	          <li>x1..x31 + PC (hard-coded numbers 1..32)</li>
441	          <li>FPR f0..f31 (if FP flag)</li>
442	          <li>13 M-mode CSRs + 16 pmpcfg + 64 pmpaddr</li>
443	          <li>v0..v31 as <code>vlenb</code>-byte payloads + 6 V CSRs (if V flag)</li>
444	        </ul>
445	      </div>
446	      <div class="card">
447	        <h4>Continue and propagate</h4>
448	        <p>After <code>sess.cont()</code>, the parent <code>waitpid()</code>s and returns QEMU2's exit code. If QEMU2 dies before the gdbstub port becomes reachable (bad <code>--qemu-binary</code> path), <code>ChildExitedDuringConnect</code> surfaces that status instead of hanging.</p>
449	      </div>
450	    </div>
451	    <div class="file-ref">verilator/src/hybrid/qemu_handback.hpp, gdbstub_session.hpp, reg_names.h</div>
452	  </details>
453	
454	  <details>
455	    <summary><span class="tag abi">ABI</span> hybrid_state_v1 - the wire contract</summary>
456	    <div class="grid">
457	      <div class="card">
458	        <h4>Single source of truth</h4>
459	        <p><code>include/hybrid/state_abi.h</code> defines the binary layout. Both the QEMU plugin (C) and vsim (C++) include this header. Layout is locked by <code>state_abi_check.h</code> static_asserts.</p>
460	      </div>
461	      <div class="card">
462	        <h4>Versioning</h4>
463	        <ul>
464	          <li>Magic: <code>0x42594841</code> ('AHYB')</li>
465	          <li>Current version: 1</li>
466	          <li>Forward-compat: never repurpose offsets in v1 - grow via <code>reserved[232]</code> or introduce v2 alongside.</li>
467	        </ul>
468	      </div>
469	      <div class="card">
470	        <h4>Flags</h4>
471	        <ul>
472	          <li><code>HYBRID_FLAG_RV64</code> - always set</li>
473	          <li><code>HYBRID_FLAG_FP</code> - set only if QEMU advertised D-extension and FPR handles bound</li>
474	          <li><code>HYBRID_FLAG_V</code> - set only if QEMU exposed vlenb &gt; 0</li>
475	        </ul>
476	        <p>Receivers MUST check flags before consuming the matching state blocks.</p>
477	      </div>
478	      <div class="card">
479	        <h4>Sizing</h4>
480	        <p><code>HYBRID_VLEN_BYTES_MAX = 64</code> (VLEN=512). Driven by <code>NDS_VLEN</code> in <code>data/configs/ax45mpv_premium.cfg</code> - changing the configured VLEN means updating this constant in lock-step.</p>
481	      </div>
482	    </div>
483	    <div class="file-ref">include/hybrid/state_abi.h, include/hybrid/state_abi_check.h</div>
484	  </details>
