486	  <details>
487	    <summary><span class="tag abi">ABI</span> V-state transport - the trickiest piece</summary>
488	    <div class="grid">
489	      <div class="card">
490	        <h4>Why scalar V CSRs are split</h4>
491	        <p><b>Tier A (Abstract):</b> vstart, vxsat, vxrm, vcsr, mstatus.VS - plain CSR writes work because they have no architectural side effect on vtype/vl.</p>
492	        <p><b>Tier B (Program Buffer):</b> vtype and vl must come from <code>vsetvl x0, x5, x6</code>. A direct csrrw to vtype sets <code>vill</code>; vl is read-only outside of vsetvl. Only vsetvl restores both atomically.</p>
493	      </div>
494	      <div class="card">
495	        <h4>Why V data regs need a scratch region</h4>
496	        <p>The RISC-V Debug Spec does not allocate Abstract Command slots for v0..v31, and the AX45MPV CPU wrapper exports no DPI probe for the V regfile.</p>
497	        <p>Workaround: a reserved 2 KiB region at <code>kVScratchGpa</code> inside the shared mmap. The fixture's prologue executes <code>vle8.v vN, (t0)</code> from scratch on entry; epilogue <code>vse8.v vN, (t0)</code> on exit. vsim reads the bytes back from the host-mapped pointer (<code>read_v_from_scratch</code>).</p>
498	      </div>
499	      <div class="card">
500	        <h4>kVScratchGpa selection</h4>
501	        <p><code>0x00FF0000</code> on <code>-M andes_ae350</code>, <code>0x80FF0000</code> on <code>-M virt</code>. Chosen as RAM_BASE + 0xFF0000 so the C stack (rt_c.ld places <code>_stack</code> at RAM_BASE + 0x700000) has ~9 MiB of headroom before colliding.</p>
502	      </div>
503	      <div class="card">
504	        <h4>Restore ordering recap</h4>
505	        <p>The strict ResumeDriver order exists because every step depends on the previous one.</p>
506	        <pre style="margin:0; background:var(--code-bg); border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; padding:8px; font-size:11px; overflow-x:auto">mstatus.VS = state.mstatus & 0x600
507	write x5 = state.vl     (Abstract)
508	write x6 = state.vtype  (Abstract)
509	PB: vsetvl x0, x5, x6   (atomic vtype+vl; resets vstart)
510	vstart = state.vstart
511	vxsat / vxrm / vcsr
512	GPRs x1..x31 (overwrites x5/x6)
513	DPC = state.pc
514	mtvec, resume</pre>
515	      </div>
516	    </div>
517	    <div class="file-ref">verilator/src/hybrid/v_regfile_xfer.hpp, resume_driver.hpp; fixtures: verilator/hybrid/test/rt_c_v_*.c</div>
518	  </details>
